segments:
V. 7. Wo to the world because of offences-That is, unspeakable misery will be in the world through them; 

  for it must needs be that offences come-Such is the nature of things, and such the weakness, folly, and wickedness of mankind, that it cannot be but they will come; 

  but wo to that man-That is, miserable is that man, 

  by whom the offence cometh.  Offences are, all things whereby any one is turned out of, or hindered in the way of God.
